            "title_weight": "500",
            "title_mb": 14,
            "body_text": "<p>The 4 Cs of diamonds (cut, colour, clarity and carat) are the universal standards used to understand diamond quality. Each C represents a unique characteristic that contributes to a diamond’s beauty and brilliance.</p><p><strong>Cut:</strong> Graded from Ideal to Poor on the IGI scale.<br/><strong>Colour:</strong> Graded from D (colourless) to Z (light yellow or brown).<br/><strong>Clarity:</strong> Graded from Flawless (FL) to Included (I3).<br/><strong>Carat:</strong> Measured in metric carats, where one carat equals 200 milligrams.</p>",
