            "title": "Diamond Colour",
            "title_color": "#111111",
            "title_size_d": 26,
            "title_size_m": 22,
            "title_weight": "500",
            "title_mb": 14,
            "body_text": "<p>Diamond colour refers to the absence of colour in a diamond. The less colour a diamond has, the rarer and more valuable it becomes. IGI grades diamond colour on a scale from <strong>D (Colourless) to Z (Light Yellow or Brown)</strong>, with each grade representing a subtle difference in colour appearance.</p><p>The IGI Colour Grading Scale includes:</p><ul><li><strong>D – F: Colourless</strong><br/>Diamonds in this range have exceptional transparency and appear completely colourless.</li><li><strong>G – J: Near Colourless</strong><br/>These diamonds show minimal colour that is difficult to notice, offering excellent value and beauty.</li><li><strong>K – M: Faint Colour</strong><br/>A slight warm tone becomes more visible while maintaining attractive brilliance.</li><li><strong>N – R: Very Light Colour</strong><br/>Noticeable colour tones begin to appear within the diamond.</li><li><strong>S – Z: Light Colour</strong><br/>Diamonds display visible yellow or brown hues.</li></ul><p>Diamond colour selection depends on personal preference, diamond size, shape, and the jewellery setting. Larger diamonds and certain shapes may reveal colour more easily, making the right grade an important part of choosing the perfect diamond.</p>",
            "text_color": "#444444",
            "text_size_d": 15,
            "text_size_m": 13,
            "text_weight": "400",
            "text_lh": "1.6",
            "text_mb": 10,
            "show_callout": false,
            "callout_text": "Good quality cut which reflects some light while maintaining weight.",
            "callout_bg": "#1b3b36",
