            "title": "Diamond Clarity",
            "title_color": "#111111",
            "title_size_d": 26,
            "title_size_m": 22,
            "title_weight": "500",
            "title_mb": 14,
            "body_text": "<p>Clarity refers to how free a diamond is from internal characteristics (<strong>inclusions</strong>) and external imperfections (<strong>blemishes</strong>). A diamond with higher clarity has fewer visible characteristics, allowing its natural beauty and brilliance to shine.</p><p>The IGI clarity scale ranges from <strong>Flawless (FL) to Included (I3)</strong>, with each grade representing the level of internal and surface features within the diamond. Most diamonds contain tiny characteristics that are not visible to the naked eye and do not affect their overall beauty.</p><p>The impact of inclusions depends on their <strong>size, number, and location</strong>. Features positioned beneath the top surface of the diamond may affect appearance more than those located near the edges. Each diamond has a unique clarity profile, making individual evaluation an important part of selecting the perfect stone.</p>",
            "text_color": "#444444",
